  data:  # adc7
    kind: work_item  # adc7
    title: "Kind-conditioned writer at scale: 194 of 312 (kind,field) cells are 100% NULL across 5 introspection fields; needs per-(kind,field) writer-contract validator"  # adc7
    status: todo_hard  # adc7
    priority: 2  # adc7
    parent: INV-virik-zobok-rakiv-lujop-budot-haduv-vimol-pigoj  # adc7
    tags:  # adc7
    - dogfooding  # adc7
    - schema_drift  # adc7
    - fold_audit_2026_06_03  # adc7
    isbefore: []  # adc7
    duplicate_of: []  # adc7
    not_duplicate_of: []  # adc7
    pr_ref:  # adc7
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family H). Consolidates F23.7 + F26.10 + F27.10 + F28.4 previously folded onto INV-virik. Full evidence remains across multiple INV-virik discussion entries (pass-23 through pass-29 batches); this row provides discrete representation as a scope-extension distinct from INV-virik's \"binary-empty-reserved-field\" framing.\n\nThe audit's verdict: kind-conditioned writer at scale is a STRUCTURAL pattern — schema declares fields universally; writers populate them only conditionally on kind. The validator's writer-contract class catches per-AR field gaps; per-(kind, field) gaps slip through. Distinct fix-site from INV-virik's scope (which is about reserved fields that are never populated by anyone — this row is about fields populated unevenly conditional on Symbol.kind).\n\n## Symptom\n\nAcross 5 introspection fields (`fingerprint`, `shape_id`, `qualified_name`, `docstring`, `signature`) × 26 Symbol kinds = 312 (kind, field) cells. Pass-29 enumeration: **194 of 312 cells (62.2%) are 100%-NULL.** Pass-23 / pass-27 / pass-28 evidence:\n\n- **shape_id 99.94% NULL on variable kind** (1608/1609 variables lack shape_id, despite being declarations) — F23.7\n- **fingerprint 21.38% NULL on method kind** (3911/18290), 0% on class, 1.83% on function — F23.7\n- **stable_id 100% NULL on 8 synthetic kinds** (enum, struct, trait, protocol, contract, event, constructor, modifier, alias) — F27.10\n- **stable_id 60% NULL on call_site** — F27.10\n- **108 nodes have stable_id=None AND language=None jointly** (cohort overlap structural) — F26.10\n- **5 introspection fields universally NULL on synthetic kinds** (external_symbol, call_site, package) — F28.4\n\nThe pattern: schema declares fields universally as `Optional[T]`; producer writers apply them only conditionally on `kind`; the condition is undocumented in spec.md.\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor each Symbol field declared in the dataclass, the spec.md documents a per-kind applicability matrix:\n\n```\nfield         | function | method | class | variable | external | call_site | ...\nfingerprint   | 100%     | 79%    | 100%  | 0%       | 0%       | 40%       | ...\nshape_id      | ...      | ...    | ...   | 0.06%    | 0%       | 0%        | ...\n```\n\nValidator checks each populated cell against the matrix. Currently the schema's `Optional[T]` declaration says \"may be None\" without specifying when None is expected vs unexpected.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nTwo parts:\n\n**(a) Per-(kind, field) writer-contract validator.** Extend WI-kafar's validator class to enforce a kind-applicability matrix. Producer adds a kind → field-set mapping at write time; consumer validates against it. Catches future regressions where a field that was 100% populated drops on some kind.\n\n**(b) Spec.md kind-applicability table.** Document the expected per-(kind, field) population. Currently the agent must grep substrate to discover the table.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F23.7** — INV-virik discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-23 batch).\n- **F26.10** — INV-virik discussion entry 2026-06-03 (pass-26 batch; joint stable_id+language NULL on synthetic kinds).\n- **F27.10** — INV-virik discussion entry 2026-06-02T22:XX (pass-27 batch; 8 synthetic kinds + 60% call_site).\n- **F28.4** — INV-virik discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-28 batch; 5 introspection fields universal NULL).\n- **F29.3** — pass-29 supporting (per-(kind, field) matrix 312 cells, 194 100%-NULL).\n\nLab notebooks: passes 23, 26, 27, 28, 29 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- **INV-virik** (existing parent — reserved-provenance META; this row is a structurally distinct mechanism within scope).\n- Sibling: **WI-spec-supply-chain-shape-drift** (Family H — spec drift on a related schema field).\n- Sibling: **WI-entrypoint-record-provenance** (Family H — EP records lack provenance fields entirely).\n- Cousin: **WI-kafar** (CI validator gate; this row's fix would land as an extended validator class)."  # adc7
    fields: {}  # adc7
